### What are common mistakes with repositories?

The most common mistake is leaking persistence concerns into the service or controller layer.

```java
package com.bank.service;

import com.bank.model.Trade;
import jakarta.persistence.EntityManager;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import java.util.List;

@Service
public class TradeMistakeService {

    // WRONG: service depends on EntityManager (JPA-specific)
    // private final EntityManager em;
    // public List<Trade> findSettled(String accountId) {
    //     return em.createQuery(...).getResultList();
    //     // Service is coupled to JPA. Cannot mock easily.
    // }

    // CORRECT: service depends on repository interface
    private final com.bank.repository.TradeRepository tradeRepo;

    public TradeMistakeService(com.bank.repository.TradeRepository tradeRepo) {
        this.tradeRepo = tradeRepo;
    }

    public List<Trade> findSettled(String accountId) {
        return tradeRepo.findSettledByAccountId(accountId);
        // Service has zero imports of JPA or EntityManager.
        // Easy to mock. Easy to swap implementation.
    }
}
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

A senior engineer knows that the Repository pattern is not just about separating SQL from business logic. It is about defining a contract between the domain layer and the infrastructure layer. The repository interface uses domain language (`findSettledByAccountId`) not database language (`SELECT * FROM trades WHERE...`).

```java
package com.bank.repository;

import com.bank.model.Trade;
import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.util.List;

// Domain-oriented naming (Repository):
public interface TradeRepository {
    List<Trade> findSettledByAccountId(String accountId);
    List<Trade> findPendingForSettlementDate(LocalDate date);
    BigDecimal calculateTotalExposure(String accountId);
}

// Data-oriented naming (DAO):
// public interface TradeDao {
//     List<Trade> selectByAccountIdAndStatus(String id, String status);
//     List<Trade> selectByDateAndStatus(LocalDate date, String status);
//     BigDecimal sumAmountByAccountId(String id);
// }
```
